        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: West Texas, High Plains, Trans-Pecos, Western High Plains, Llano Estacado\n- Concepts: Buda Limestone, geological formations, Late Cretaceous\n\nFacts:\n- The Buda Limestone is a geological formation in the High Plains and Trans-Pecos regions of West Texas.\n- The strata of the Buda Limestone date back to the Late Cretaceous.\n- The southern region of the Western High Plains ecology region contains the geological formation known as Llano Estacado.\n- Llano Estacado can be seen from a short distance or on satellite maps.",
